accel/tcg: a 64k-entry jump cache that flushes in O(fills).

The guest profile of a Home-screen swipe executed 575k distinct
translation blocks in 14 s at 4.3 instructions per TB, with ~200 block
starts in each hot 4 KiB page. helper_lookup_tb_ptr's per-vCPU jump cache
had 4096 entries in 64 page buckets of 64 slots each (pc bits 0-5 xor
6-11, so word-aligned A64 starts shared slots four ways within a page):
indirect branches, returns and every branch out of a page that missed it
paid get_page_addr_code plus a QHT probe, ~100 ns against ~10 ns for a hit
(tests/engine/branch-bench.S "wide": 8192 BLR targets).

- TB_JMP_CACHE_BITS 12 -> 16 (1 MiB per vCPU), 512 slots per page bucket
  (pc >> 2 folded with the bits above it) and 128 buckets chosen by a
  Fibonacci hash of the page number. The page/slot split is kept, so
  tb_jmp_cache_clear_page still clears exactly the slots a page can use.
- A full flush (every TLB flush; an ASID change in TTBR0 is one) used to
  clear all entries; the owner now logs the indices it fills
  (TB_JMP_CACHE_LOG = 4096) and clears only those. Only the owning vCPU
  fills entries or trusts the log; any other caller (reset, tb_flush in an
  exclusive section) clears everything, as before. tlb_flush_range uses the
  full flush beyond 16 pages instead of clearing 1024 slots per page.
- tb_jmp_cache_inval_tb no longer clears every vCPU's whole cache per
  invalidated CF_PCREL TB (arm always uses CF_PCREL): a code-page write
  invalidating N TBs cost N full clears of every cache. do_tb_phys_invalidate
  sets CF_INVALID first, every jump-cache user compares tb_cflags() against
  cflags that never contain it, and TB memory is only reclaimed by tb_flush,
  which clears all caches.
- Read-only accel properties jmp-cache-misses (found in the QHT),
  jmp-cache-absent (nothing found: a translation follows) and
  jmp-cache-flushes, summed over the vCPUs (qom-get /machine/accel), for
  measuring a live guest. Hits are not counted.

tests/engine/branch-bench.S (virt, -cpu max, 1 CPU, best of 7, ns per
iteration, host loaded by a running phone): wide 78 -> 58, smc 107 -> 95;
the hit-only phases unchanged. tests/engine/jump-cache-probe.S (MMU on:
remapped pages after TLBI VAE1, TLBI VMALLE1 and an ASID change, a direct
cross-page exit, rewritten code) gives the stock QEMU results.

